---
import TimerPage from '@/layouts/TimerPage.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import { faqs } from '@/data/faqs';
import { relatedTimers, relatedPosts } from '@/data/related';
import { defaultConfigs } from '@/engine/presets';
import { meditations } from '@/data/meditations';
---

<TimerPage
  title="Meditation Timer – One Soft Bell, Screen Stays On"
  description="Free meditation timer: one soft bell every 10 minutes for 30 minutes, or any interval you set. No ticks, no alarm. Screen stays awake, works offline."
  path="/meditation"
  h1="Meditation timer"
  lede="One soft bell every 10 minutes for 30 minutes, then one to finish. Change the interval or the length. Nothing else makes a sound."
  config={defaultConfigs.meditation}
  faq={faqs['/meditation']}
  related={relatedTimers['/meditation']!}
  posts={relatedPosts['/meditation']}
  crumbName="Meditation timer"
>
  <Section num="01" title="How it is different" flush>
    <p>
      The other timers on this site are built to be noticed: a rising pair for work, a falling pair
      for rest, ticks for the last three seconds. This one is built to be forgotten. There is one
      bell. It rings once when the sit begins after a short settle-in, once at each interval, and
      once at the end. Between bells the page is silent and the digits are the only thing that
      moves.
    </p>
    <p>
      The default is a 30 minute sit with a bell every 10 minutes. That gives three blocks, which is
      enough structure for a body scan, then breath, then open awareness, or simply three reminders
      to come back. Set Bell every equal to Total for a single bell at the end.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section num="02" title="Presets">
    <p>Each length has its own page with the bells already placed.</p>
    <ul>
      {meditations.map((m) => (
        <li>
          <a href={m.path}>{m.h1}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </Section>
  <Section num="03" title="Screen, sound, silence">
    <p>
      The timer asks the phone or laptop to keep the screen awake while it runs, so the display does
      not go dark and the sit does not end with a locked phone. Turn the brightness down by hand if
      you want a dim room. The bell is generated in the browser, so there is nothing to download and
      it works with no connection after the first visit.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you would rather sit in the dark with the phone face down, that works too: the timing is
      based on timestamps, so the bell lands on the right second as long as the page stays open.
      Mute is available for a fully silent sit where you only glance at the digits.
    </p>
  </Section>
</TimerPage>
